
// draft
tail(n: Int, iterable: Text[]) -> Text[]
	note "return the last n items of the iterable, in their original order"
	# The output is the items of the iterable from position (the item count minus n) up to the end,
	# in their original order.
	// example wanted: n 3 over ["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"], the docstring case: the last three
	// items are kept
	// example wanted: n 0 over a non-empty list: the start position equals the item count, so the
	// slice is empty
	// example wanted: n larger than the item count: the start position is negative and clamps to 0,
	// so the slice is the whole list
	// example wanted: an empty iterable with n 2: there is nothing to slice
	// example wanted: n -1 over ["A","B"]: the start is past the end, so the slice claim reads it
	// as empty; decide whether negative n is an error case, since Python's sized path gives empty
	// and its unsized deque path raises ValueError
	// example wanted: duplicates, n 1 over ["A","B","A"]: the slice is positional, so the kept "A"
	// is the last occurrence, not the first
